# The USB audio's layout (0.16.25, the USB & MIDI page's fourth knob, Audio): Mix (2 channels, as before), Parts (drums, bass, acid, pluck, pad L, pad R),
# Parts 2 (bass, acid, pluck, pad, the synths' effects L R), Parts 3 (kick, snare, clap, hats, perc, the drums' effects; 2026-11-11) and Set (the mix, drums, bass, acid + pluck, pad). A new layout is stored in the global record at once and sent to the port (which lets go and comes
# back so the host reads it); the page says what each channel carries; it comes back after a power cycle.
seed 0
wait 3000
expect usbaudio 0
expect usbaudioport 0
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 7
wait 100
expect fxpage 24
shot usbaudio_mix.png
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect usbaudio 1
expect usbaudioport 1
expect usbreconnects 1
shot usbaudio_parts.png
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect usbaudio 2
expect usbaudioport 2
expect usbreconnects 2
shot usbaudio_parts2.png
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect usbaudio 3
expect usbaudioport 3
expect usbreconnects 3
shot usbaudio_parts3.png
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect usbaudio 4
expect usbaudioport 4
expect usbreconnects 4
shot usbaudio_set.png
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect usbaudio 4
expect usbreconnects 4
tap FX
wait 2000
# kept through a power cycle
reboot
wait 3000
expect usbaudio 4
